Independent review of BankLedger's skinning adoption (M2), with the fixes.

Findings and outcomes:
1. MAJOR, fixed in 65c8ae8 (BL-04): NS.SkinPickerSpec passed page = "General", the display name. The library matches the registered key "general" exactly, so the gear opened the landing page and SelectTab found no panel (SKIN-22). Now page = "general". tests/test_skin_picker.lua reads the key from settings/Panel.lua's RegisterOptionsPage call and the panel's pageKey instead of pinning a literal. Confirmed red against the old value.
2. minor, fixed in 138c643 (BL-02): after a live switch back to Ka0s Default the close art kept the other skin's close.rest, because S.CloseButton saves no prior tint for P.unpaint. Composed around it in the host: a weak list of close controls plus an OnLooksChanged listener that re-tints from bl.closeRest (a no-op under every other skin). There is a new round-trip test, confirmed red first. library_gap: CloseButton does not save the art's prior tint for P.unpaint.
3. minor, fixed in c864a3f (BL-02): BindRow built the group header's count escape with NS.SkinEscape on every bind. It is now COUNT_ESC, resolved in LT.ReskinColors. A new test checks that no token is read per bind, confirmed red first.
4. minor, fixed in efbf369 (BL-02): the close fallback glyph's typed STANDARD_TEXT_FONT now gets NS.Skin.Font(x) after the stock SetFont, the same pattern Export and InsightsWidgets use. There is a new test, confirmed red first. Declined: extending the literal gate to SetFont, which is out of scope for this fix.
5. minor, DECLINED: the Minimum quality labels (core/Constants.lua qualityHex, allow-list E4) still use the client's ITEM_QUALITY_COLORS. Moving them to q.* would change Ka0s Default by one byte on poor, rare and epic (the library's written-out q.* values are 0.62/0.44,0.87/0.64,0.21,0.93, against the client's 9d/70dd/a335ee), which breaks the rule that Ka0s Default looks exactly as today. It would also need a settings-page rebuild hook. E4 stays recorded. This is left as a decision for the execution record.
6. minor, DECLINED here: BL-RV d66414f carries the trailer of the earlier stuck session (session_01JV4dmMQQ4HwqVN5saduTPG). A reword would rewrite every commit after it, so it is left for the owner to decide before push.

